msgstr "平權估計圖 - 假陽性率平權"

msgid ""
"<b>Figure %1$i.</b> Estimated parity statistics (i.e., the ratio of true "
"positive rate from each unprivileged group to the privileged %2$s group) for "
"all groups in the data. The closer the parity lies to one, the less "
"discrimination occurs in the algorithm."
msgstr "<b>圖 %1$i。</b> 資料中所有群體之估計平權統計量（即各未受優惠群體相對於受優惠 %2$s 群體之真陽性率比率）。平權愈接近一，表示演算法中發生的歧視愈少。"

msgid "Prior and Posterior Distribution Plot"
msgstr "先驗與後驗分布圖"

msgid ""
"<b>Figure %1$i.</b> The prior and posterior distributions on the log odds "
"ratio for each unprivileged group compared to the privileged group (%2$s)."
msgstr "<b>圖 %1$i。</b> 各未受優惠群體相對於受優惠群體 (%2$s) 之對數勝算比的先驗與後驗分布。"

msgid ""
"As the measures are significantly different from each other, we can conclude "
"that this algorithm is unfair against the unprivileged group(s)."
msgstr "由於各指標彼此顯著不同，我們可推論此演算法對未受優惠群體不公平。"

msgid ""
"As the measures are not significantly different from each other, we cannot "
"conclude that this algorithm is unfair against the unprivileged group(s)."
msgstr "由於各指標彼此未顯著不同，我們無法推論此演算法對未受優惠群體不公平。"

msgid ""
"The <i>p</i>-values are %1$s and %2$s and the null hypothesis of equal %3$s "
"and %4$s across protected groups %5$s. %6$s"
msgstr "<i>p</i> 值為 %1$s 及 %2$s，且各受保護群體間之 %3$s 與 %4$s 相等的虛無假設 %5$s。%6$s"

msgid ""
"The <i>p</i>-value is %1$s and the null hypothesis of equal %2$s across "
"protected groups %3$s. %4$s"
msgstr "<i>p</i> 值為 %1$s，且各受保護群體間之 %2$s 相等的虛無假設 %3$s。%4$s"

msgid ""
"The goal of this procedure is to determine to what extent the predictions of "
"an algorithm are fair towards protected groups on a sensitive attribute. "
"Fairness -or discrimination- can be quantified using so-called fairness "
"measures. There are various fairness measures, and different measures can "
"lead to different conclusions about fairness. Therefore, selecting the most "
"appropriate fairness measure for the context at hand is crucial. The "
"decision-making workflow allows for determining the most suitable fairness "
"measure by answering the necessary questions."
msgstr "此程序的目標在於判定演算法之預測在敏感屬性上對於受保護群體是否公平。公平性（或歧視性）可使用所謂的公平性指標加以量化。公平性指標有許多種，而不同的指標可能導致關於公平性的不同結論。因此，針對當下情境選擇最適當的公平性指標至關重要。決策工作流程允許透過回答必要問題來決定最合適的公平性指標。"

msgid "<u>Selection</u>"
msgstr "<u>選擇</u>"

msgid "<u>Evaluation</u>"
msgstr "<u>評估</u>"

msgid "The most suitable fairness measure is <b>%1$s</b>."
msgstr "最合適的公平性指標為 <b>%1$s</b>。"

msgid ""
"<u>Definition of Fairness:</u>\n"
"The algorithm is fair if its use results in the same ratio of items from two "
"different groups experiencing a change in the status quo (i.e., being "
"classified as positive). The term items refers to what is being classified; "
"these items can be people, like job applicants, or objects, such as bank "
"accounts.\n"
"\n"
"<u>Formula:</u>\n"
"Disparate impact is obtained by dividing the positive rate of the "
"unprivileged group by that of the privileged group. The positive rate is "
"equal to (TP+FP)/N, where TP denotes true positives (items correctly "
"classified as positive), FP denotes false positives (items incorrectly "
"classified as positive), and N represents the total number of items "
"classified by the algorithm.\n"
"\n"
"<u>Further Details:</u>\n"
"The most common use of disparate impact is linked to the U.S. Equal "
"Employment Opportunity Commission (EEOC) guidelines, particularly the %1$s%% "
"rule. According to this rule, if disparate impact is higher than 0.80, there "
"is no discrimination. This method has limitations, as the threshold value is "
"not based on the measure's properties, data characteristics, or statistical "
"considerations. Originally derived from U.S. employment hiring rates, the "
"rule lacks theoretical rigor for broader applications."
msgstr "<u>公平性之定義：</u>\n該演算法若其使用導致來自兩個不同群體之項目經歷現狀改變（即被分類為陽性）的比率相同，即為公平。『項目』一詞指被分類的對象；這些項目可以是人（如求職者）或物件（如銀行帳戶）。\n\n<u>公式：</u>\n差異影響係將未受優惠群體之陽性率除以受優惠群體之陽性率而得。陽性率等於 (TP+FP)/N，其中 TP 表示真陽性（被正確分類為陽性的項目）、FP 表示假陽性（被不正確分類為陽性的項目）、N 表示演算法分類之項目總數。\n\n<u>進一步細節：</u>\n差異影響最常見的用途與美國平等就業機會委員會 (EEOC) 的指導方針有關，特別是 %1$s%% 規則。根據此規則，若差異影響高於 0.80，則不構成歧視。此方法有其限制，因為門檻值並非基於該指標的特性、資料特徵或統計考量。該規則最初源自美國雇用率，缺乏適用於更廣泛情境的理論嚴謹性。"

msgid ""
"<u>Definition of Fairness:</u>\n"
"The algorithm is fair if its use results in the same number of items from "
"different groups experiencing correct and incorrect changes in the status "
"quo (i.e, being, correctly and incorrectly, classified as positive). The "
"term items refers to what is being classified; these items can be people, "
"like job applicants, or objects, such as bank accounts.\n"
"\n"
"<u>Formula:</u>\n"
"Equalized odds combines the true positive rate (TPR) and the false positive "
"rate (FPR). The TPR is calculated as TP/(TP+FP) and the FPR as FP/(TN+FP), "
"applied to both privileged and unprivileged groups. Here, TP denotes true "
"positives (correctly classified positive items), TN denotes true negatives "
"(correctly classified negative items), and FP denotes false positives "
"(incorrectly classified positive items).\n"
"\n"
"<u>Further Details:</u>\n"
"It is important to note that this is the only measure in the decision-making "
"workflow that addresses both the correct classification of the positive "
"class and the incorrect classification of the negative class."
msgstr "<u>公平性之定義：</u>\n該演算法若其使用導致來自不同群體之項目經歷現狀之正確與不正確改變（即被正確與不正確地分類為陽性）的數量相同，即為公平。『項目』一詞指被分類的對象；這些項目可以是人（如求職者）或物件（如銀行帳戶）。\n\n<u>公式：</u>\n均衡機率結合了真陽性率 (TPR) 與假陽性率 (FPR)。TPR 計算為 TP/(TP+FP)，FPR 計算為 FP/(TN+FP)，並同時套用於受優惠與未受優惠群體。此處 TP 表示真陽性（被正確分類的陽性項目）、TN 表示真陰性（被正確分類的陰性項目）、FP 表示假陽性（被不正確分類的陽性項目）。\n\n<u>進一步細節：</u>\n請務必注意，這是決策工作流程中唯一同時處理陽性類別之正確分類與陰性類別之不正確分類的指標。"

msgid ""
"<u>Definition of Fairness:</u>\n"
"The algorithm is fair if its use results in the same number of items from "
"different groups experiencing correct changes in the status quo (i.e., being "
"correctly classified as positive). The term items refers to what is being "
"classified; these items can be people, like job applicants, or objects, such "
"as bank accounts.\n"
"\n"
"<u>Formula:</u>\n"
"Predictive rate parity is based on precision, calculated as TP/(TP+FP), "
"applied to both the privileged and unprivileged groups. Here, TP denotes "
"true positives (correctly classified positive items) and FP denotes false "
"positives (incorrectly classified positive items)."
msgstr "<u>公平性之定義：</u>\n該演算法若其使用導致來自不同群體之項目經歷現狀之正確改變（即被正確分類為陽性）的數量相同，即為公平。『項目』一詞指被分類的對象；這些項目可以是人（如求職者）或物件（如銀行帳戶）。\n\n<u>公式：</u>\n預測率平權以精確度為基礎，計算為 TP/(TP+FP)，並同時套用於受優惠與未受優惠群體。此處 TP 表示真陽性（被正確分類的陽性項目），FP 表示假陽性（被不正確分類的陽性項目）。"

msgid ""
"<u>Definition of Fairness:</u>\n"
"The algorithm is fair if its use results in the same number of items from "
"different groups experiencing correct changes in the status quo (i.e., being "
"correctly classified as positive). The term items refers to what is being "
"classified; these items can be people, like job applicants, or objects, such "
"as bank accounts.\n"
"\n"
"<u>Formula:</u>\n"
"Equal opportunity is based on the true positive rate, calculated as TP/"
"(TP+FN), applied to both privileged and unprivileged groups. Here, TP "
"denotes true positives (correctly classified positive items) and FN denotes "
"false negatives (incorrectly classified negative items)."
msgstr "<u>公平性之定義：</u>\n該演算法若其使用導致來自不同群體之項目經歷現狀之正確改變（即被正確分類為陽性）的數量相同，即為公平。『項目』一詞指被分類的對象；這些項目可以是人（如求職者）或物件（如銀行帳戶）。\n\n<u>公式：</u>\n平等機會以真陽性率為基礎，計算為 TP/(TP+FN)，並同時套用於受優惠與未受優惠群體。此處 TP 表示真陽性（被正確分類的陽性項目），FN 表示假陰性（被不正確分類的陰性項目）。"

msgid ""
"<u>Definition of Fairness:</u>\n"
"The algorithm is fair if its use results in the same number of items from "
"different groups correctly experiencing no changes in the status quo (i.e., "
"being correctly classified as negative). The term items refers to what is "
"being classified; these items can be people, like job applicants, or "
"objects, such as bank accounts.\n"
"\n"
"<u>Formula:</u>\n"
"Specificity parity is based on the true negative rate, calculated as TN/"
"(TN+FP), applied to both privileged and unprivileged groups. Here, TN "
"denotes true negatives (correctly classified negative items) and FP denotes "
"false positives (incorrectly classified positive items)."
msgstr "<u>公平性之定義：</u>\n該演算法若其使用導致來自不同群體之項目正確地經歷現狀無改變（即被正確分類為陰性）的數量相同，即為公平。『項目』一詞指被分類的對象；這些項目可以是人（如求職者）或物件（如銀行帳戶）。\n\n<u>公式：</u>\n特異性平權以真陰性率為基礎，計算為 TN/(TN+FP)，並同時套用於受優惠與未受優惠群體。此處 TN 表示真陰性（被正確分類的陰性項目），FP 表示假陽性（被不正確分類的陽性項目）。"

msgid ""
"<u>Definition of Fairness:</u>\n"
"The algorithm is fair if its use results in the same number of items from "
"different groups correctly experiencing no changes in the status quo (i.e., "
"being correctly classified as negative). The term items refers to what is "
"being classified; these items can be people, like job applicants, or "
"objects, such as bank accounts.\n"
"\n"
"<u>Formula:</u>\n"
"Negative predictive value parity is based on the negative predictive value, "
"calculated as TN/(TN+FN), applied to both privileged and unprivileged "
"groups. Here, TN denotes true negatives (correctly classified negative "
"items) and FN denotes false negatives (incorrectly classified negative "
"items)."
msgstr "<u>公平性之定義：</u>\n該演算法若其使用導致來自不同群體之項目正確地經歷現狀無改變（即被正確分類為陰性）的數量相同，即為公平。『項目』一詞指被分類的對象；這些項目可以是人（如求職者）或物件（如銀行帳戶）。\n\n<u>公式：</u>\n陰性預測值平權以陰性預測值為基礎，計算為 TN/(TN+FN)，並同時套用於受優惠與未受優惠群體。此處 TN 表示真陰性（被正確分類的陰性項目），FN 表示假陰性（被不正確分類的陰性項目）。"

msgid ""
"<u>Definition of Fairness:</u>\n"
"The algorithm is fair if its use results in the same number of items from "
"different groups correctly experiencing changes and correctly experiencing "
"no changes in the status quo (i.e., being correctly classified as positive "
"and being correctly classified as negative). The term items refers to what "
"is being classified; these items can be people, like job applicants, or "
"objects, such as bank accounts.\n"
"\n"
"<u>Formula:</u>\n"
"Accuracy parity is based on accuracy, calculated as (TP+TN)/N, applied to "
"both privileged and unprivileged groups. Here, TP denotes true positives "
"(correctly classified positive items), TN denotes true negatives (correctly "
"classified negative items), and N represents the total number of items "
"classified by the algorithm. The sum of TP and TN reflects the total number "
"of correct classifications made by the algorithm.\n"
"\n"
"<u>Further Details:</u>\n"
"Accuracy parity, like accuracy as a model evaluation metric, has a major "
"flaw when applied to cases where the positive class is a small minority. For "
"example, if %1$s%% of the privileged group and %2$s%% of the unprivileged "
"group commit fraud, accuracy may seem high overall (%3$s%%), but masks "
"disparities, with the unprivileged group having lower accuracy (%4$s%%) "
"compared to the privileged group (%5$s%%). Unlike other measures, accuracy "
"parity does not consider varying error costs. It fails to detect increases "
"in false negatives or false positives, missing the associated rise in costs."
msgstr "<u>公平性之定義：</u>\n該演算法若其使用導致來自不同群體之項目正確地經歷改變與正確地經歷現狀無改變（即被正確分類為陽性以及被正確分類為陰性）的數量相同，即為公平。『項目』一詞指被分類的對象；這些項目可以是人（如求職者）或物件（如銀行帳戶）。\n\n<u>公式：</u>\n準確度平權以準確度為基礎，計算為 (TP+TN)/N，並同時套用於受優惠與未受優惠群體。此處 TP 表示真陽性（被正確分類的陽性項目）、TN 表示真陰性（被正確分類的陰性項目）、N 表示演算法分類之項目總數。TP 與 TN 之和反映演算法所做之正確分類總數。\n\n<u>進一步細節：</u>\n準確度平權如同作為模型評估指標的準確度，當套用於陽性類別僅佔少數的案例時具有重大缺陷。例如，若受優惠群體中有 %1$s%%、未受優惠群體中有 %2$s%% 犯欺詐，整體準確度可能看似很高（%3$s%%），但掩蓋了差異，其中未受優惠群體之準確度（%4$s%%）低於受優惠群體（%5$s%%）。與其他指標不同，準確度平權未考量不同的誤差成本。它無法偵測假陰性或假陽性之增加，而遺漏了隨之而來的成本上升。"

msgid ""
"<u>Definition of Fairness:</u>\n"
"The algorithm is fair if its use results in the same number of items from "
"different groups experiencing incorrect changes in the status quo (i.e., "
"being incorrectly classified as positive). The term items refers to what is "
"being classified; these items can be people, like job applicants, or "
"objects, such as bank accounts.\n"
"\n"
"<u>Formula:</u>\n"
"False positive rate parity is based on the false positive rate, calculated "
"as FP/(TN+FP), applied to both privileged and unprivileged groups. Here, FP "
"denotes false positives (incorrectly classified positive items), and TN "
"denotes true negatives (correctly classified negative items)."
msgstr "<u>公平性之定義：</u>\n該演算法若其使用導致來自不同群體之項目經歷現狀之不正確改變（即被不正確分類為陽性）的數量相同，即為公平。『項目』一詞指被分類的對象；這些項目可以是人（如求職者）或物件（如銀行帳戶）。\n\n<u>公式：</u>\n假陽性率平權以假陽性率為基礎，計算為 FP/(TN+FP)，並同時套用於受優惠與未受優惠群體。此處 FP 表示假陽性（被不正確分類的陽性項目），TN 表示真陰性（被正確分類的陰性項目）。"

msgid ""
"<u>Definition of Fairness:</u>\n"
"The algorithm is fair if its use results in the same number of items from "
"different groups incorrectly experiencing no changes in the status quo (i."
"e., being incorrectly classified as negative). The term items refers to what "
"is being classified; these items can be people, like job applicants, or "
"objects, such as bank accounts.\n"
"\n"
"<u>Formula:</u>\n"
"False negative rate parity is based on the false negative rate, calculated "
"as FN/(TP+FN), applied to both privileged and unprivileged groups. Here, FN "
"denotes false negatives (incorrectly classified negative items), and TP "
"denotes true positives (correctly classified positive items)."
msgstr "<u>公平性之定義：</u>\n該演算法若其使用導致來自不同群體之項目不正確地經歷現狀無改變（即被不正確分類為陰性）的數量相同，即為公平。『項目』一詞指被分類的對象；這些項目可以是人（如求職者）或物件（如銀行帳戶）。\n\n<u>公式：</u>\n假陰性率平權以假陰性率為基礎，計算為 FN/(TP+FN)，並同時套用於受優惠與未受優惠群體。此處 FN 表示假陰性（被不正確分類的陰性項目），TP 表示真陽性（被正確分類的陽性項目）。"

msgid "Decision-Making Workflow Plot"
msgstr "決策工作流程圖"

msgid ""
"<b>Figure %1$i.</b> Graphical representation of the decision-making "
"workflow. The label 'FP' indicates 'False Positives' and the label 'FN' "
"indicates 'False Negatives'. The white rectangles indicate the followed path "
"based on the answers provided to the necessary questions of the workflow, "
"the gray rectangles represent the ignored path."
msgstr "<b>圖 %1$i。</b> 決策工作流程之圖形表示。標籤『FP』表示『假陽性』，標籤『FN』表示『假陰性』。白色矩形表示依據對工作流程必要問題所給之答案而採用的路徑，灰色矩形表示被忽略的路徑。"

msgid ""
"This procedure analyzes the frequency with which values get repeated within "
"a data set to statistically identify whether the data were likely tampered "
"with. Unlike Benford's law, and its generalizations, this approach examines "
"the entire number at once, not only the first or last digit.\n"
"\n"
"To determine whether the data show an excessive amount of repeated values, "
"the null hypothesis that the data do not contain an unexpected amount of "
"repeated values is tested with a type-I error of %1$s. To quantify what is "
"expected, this test requires the assumption that the integer portions of the "
"numbers are not associated with their decimal portions."
msgstr "此程序分析數值在資料集內重複出現的次數，以統計方式識別資料是否可能遭竄改。與本福德定律及其推廣不同，此方法一次檢視整個數字，而不僅是首位或末位數字。\n\n為判定資料是否顯示過多重複數值，會以類型一誤差率 %1$s 檢驗資料未包含異常數量重複數值之虛無假設。為量化何謂預期情況，此檢定需要假設數字的整數部分與其小數部分無關。"

msgid "<u>Assessing repeated values</u>"
msgstr "<u>評估重複數值</u>"

msgid "<b>Table %1$i.</b> Repeated Values Test"
msgstr "<b>表 %1$i。</b> 重複數值檢定"

msgid "Average"
msgstr "平均"

msgid "Frequency"
msgstr "次數"

msgid "Entropy"
msgstr "熵"

msgid ""
"The displayed <i>p</i>-value is one-sided and is computed on the basis of "
"%1$s samples."
msgstr "顯示的 <i>p</i> 值為單尾，並以 %1$s 個樣本為基礎計算。"

msgid "<b>Table %1$i.</b> Assumption Checks"
msgstr "<b>表 %1$i。</b> 假設檢核"

msgid ""
"The displayed <i>p</i>-value is for a two-sided test against H%1$s: <i>r</i> "
"= 0."
msgstr "顯示的 <i>p</i> 值是針對 H%1$s: <i>r</i> = 0 之雙尾檢定。"

msgid "Percentage"
msgstr "百分比"

msgid "Observed vs. Expected Average Frequency"
msgstr "觀察到的平均次數與期望平均次數"

msgid "Average frequency"
msgstr "平均次數"

msgid "Simulated frequency"
msgstr "模擬次數"

msgid ""
"<b>Figure %i:</b> The expected average frequencies of values versus the "
"observed average frequency in the data set."
msgstr "<b>圖 %i：</b> 資料集中期望的各數值平均次數與觀察到的平均次數。"

msgid "Observed vs. Expected Entropy"
msgstr "觀察到的熵與期望熵"

msgid ""
"<b>Figure %i:</b> The expected entropy of values versus the observed entropy "
"in the data set."
msgstr "<b>圖 %i：</b> 資料集中期望的各數值熵與觀察到的熵。"

msgid "Histogram of Individual Values"
msgstr "個別數值之直方圖"

msgid "<b>Figure %i:</b> Histogram of the individual values in the data set."
msgstr "<b>圖 %i：</b> 資料集中個別數值之直方圖。"

msgid "%1$s < α"
msgstr "%1$s < α"

msgid "%1$s >= α"
msgstr "%1$s >= α"

msgid ""
"The <i>p</i>-value is %1$s and the null hypothesis that the data do not "
"contain an unexpected amount of repeated values %2$s."
msgstr "<i>p</i> 值為 %1$s，且資料未包含異常數量的重複數值之虛無假設 %2$s。"

msgid "percentage"
msgstr "百分比"

msgid "amount"
msgstr "數量"

msgid "<u>Planning</u>"
msgstr "<u>規劃</u>"

msgid ""
"Analysis not possible: The materiality is higher than, or equal to the total "
"value of the observations."
msgstr "無法分析：重大性高於或等於觀察值之總值。"

msgid ""
"Analysis not possible: The expected errors are equal to, or higher than, the "
"number of units in the population."
msgstr "無法分析：期望誤差等於或高於母體中的單位數。"

msgid ""
"Analysis not possible: The expected errors are higher than the performance "
"materiality."
msgstr "無法分析：期望誤差高於績效重大性。"

msgid ""
"The detection risk is equal to or higher than 100%%. Please re-specify the "
"custom values for the Inherent risk and/or Control risk and/or Analytical "
"risk, or the confidence."
msgstr "偵測風險等於或高於 100%%。請重新指定固有風險及／或控制風險及／或分析風險之自訂數值，或指定信賴水準。"

msgid ""
"You cannot incorporate this prior information into your analysis because you "
"are not testing against a performance materiality."
msgstr "由於您不是針對績效重大性進行檢定，因此無法將此先驗資訊納入您的分析。"

msgid ""
"The prior expected misstatement rate in the population is larger than the "
"performance materiality."
msgstr "母體中之期望先驗錯報率大於績效重大性。"

msgid "Selection Summary"
msgstr "選取摘要"

msgid ""
"You must specify unique item ID's. The row numbers of the data set are "
"sufficient."
msgstr "您必須指定唯一的項目 ID。資料集的列號即足夠。"

msgid "Evaluation Summary"
msgstr "評估摘要"

msgid ""
"The hypergeometric upper bound requires that you specify the number of units "
"in the population."
msgstr "超幾何上界要求您指定母體中的單位數。"

msgid ""
"The direct, difference, ratio, and regression bounds require that you "
"specify the number of items and the number of units in the population."
msgstr "直接、差異、比率及迴歸上界要求您指定母體中的項目數與單位數。"

msgid ""
"The detection risk is equal to or higher than 100%%. Please re-specify your "
"values for the Inherent risk and/or Control risk and/or Analytical risk, or "
"the confidence."
msgstr "偵測風險等於或高於 100%%。請重新指定固有風險及／或控制風險及／或分析風險之數值，或指定信賴水準。"

msgid ""
"Analysis not possible: The materiality (%1$s) is higher than, or equal to "
"the total value of the population (%2$s)."
msgstr "無法分析：重大性 (%1$s) 高於或等於母體之總值 (%2$s)。"

msgid ""
"Analysis not possible: The hurdle model cannot be applied with this specific "
"prior distribution because it is improper. Please specify a different prior "
"distribution."
msgstr "無法分析：障礙模型無法與此特定的先驗分布搭配使用，因為它是非正規 (improper) 的。請指定不同的先驗分布。"

msgid ""
"Select one or both sampling objectives to begin planning an audit sample.\n"
"\n"
"%1$s <b>Test against a performance materiality</b>\n"
"\n"
"Enable this objective if you want to test whether the total misstatement in "
"the population exceeds a certain limit (i.e., the performance materiality) "
"based on a sample. This approach allows you to plan a sample such that, when "
"the sample meets your expectations, the maximum error is said to be below "
"performance materiality. In the evaluation you will be able to quantify the "
"evidence that your sample contains for or against the statement that the "
"population misstatement does not exceed the performance materiality.\n"
"\n"
"%2$s <b>Obtain a minimum precision</b>\n"
"\n"
"Enable this objective if you want to obtain a minimum precision when "
"estimating the total misstatement in the population based on a sample. This "
"approach allows you to plan a sample such that, when the sample meets "
"expectations, the accuracy of your estimate is below a tolerable percentage. "
"In the evaluation you will be able to quantify the accuracy of your estimate "
"of the population misstatement."
msgstr "請選擇一個或兩個抽樣目標以開始規劃審計樣本。\n\n%1$s <b>針對績效重大性進行檢定</b>\n\n若您想根據樣本檢定母體中之總錯報是否超過特定上限（即績效重大性），請啟用此目標。此方法允許您規劃一個樣本，使樣本符合您的期望時，最大誤差被判定為低於績效重大性。在評估中，您將能量化樣本所提供支持或反對『母體錯報未超過績效重大性』此陳述的證據。\n\n%2$s <b>取得最小精確度</b>\n\n若您想在根據樣本估計母體中之總錯報時取得最小精確度，請啟用此目標。此方法允許您規劃一個樣本，使樣本符合期望時，您估計之準確度低於可容忍的百分比。在評估中，您將能量化您對母體錯報之估計的準確度。"

msgid ""
"The objective of this sampling procedure is to show with %1$s confidence "
"that the %2$s of misstatement in the population is lower than the "
"performance materiality of %3$s."
msgstr "此抽樣程序之目標在於以 %1$s 信賴水準顯示母體之%2$s錯報低於績效重大性 %3$s。"

msgid ""
"The objective of this sampling procedure is to estimate the misstatement in "
"the population with %1$s confidence and a minimum precision of %2$s.\n"
"\n"
"The quantity of interest is the misstatement θ in the population. "
"Misstatement is defined as the difference between an item's booked "
"(recorded) value and its audited (true) value."
msgstr "此抽樣程序之目標在於以 %1$s 信賴水準及最小精確度 %2$s 估計母體錯報。\n\n感興趣之數量為母體中的錯報 θ。錯報定義為一項目之帳面（已記錄）數值與其審計（真實）數值之差異。"

msgid ""
"The objective of this sampling procedure is to show with %1$s confidence and "
"a precision of %3$s that the %2$s of misstatement in the population is lower "
"than the performance materiality of %4$s."
msgstr "此抽樣程序之目標在於以 %1$s 信賴水準及 %3$s 之精確度，顯示母體之%2$s錯報低於績效重大性 %4$s。"

msgid "of intolerable misstatement H%1$s: %2$s %3$s %4$s"
msgstr "不可容忍錯報之 H%1$s：%2$s %3$s %4$s"

msgid "of exact misstatement H%1$s: %2$s = %3$s"
msgstr "精確錯報之 H%1$s：%2$s = %3$s"

msgid "of tolerable misstatement H%1$s: %2$s %3$s %4$s"
msgstr "可容忍錯報之 H%1$s：%2$s %3$s %4$s"

msgid "of tolerable misstatement H%1$s: %2$s < %3$s"
msgstr "可容忍錯報之 H%1$s：%2$s < %3$s"

msgid "of no misstatement H%1$s: %2$s %3$s %4$s"
msgstr "無錯報之 H%1$s：%2$s %3$s %4$s"

msgid "of intolerable misstatement H%1$s: %2$s > %3$s"
msgstr "不可容忍錯報之 H%1$s：%2$s > %3$s"

msgid ""
"%1$s\n"
"\n"
"The quantity of interest is the misstatement %2$s in the population. "
"Misstatement is defined as the difference between an item's booked "
"(recorded) value and its audit (true) value. When testing the population "
"misstatement against a given performance materiality, two statistical "
"hypotheses about %2$s are formulated:\n"
"\n"
"- The (null) hypothesis %3$s,\n"
"- The (alternative) hypothesis %4$s.\n"
"\n"
"The audit risk %5$s is the risk of incorrectly rejecting the hypothesis "
"%3$s. To reject this hypothesis on the basis of a sample, the information "
"from the sample must be sufficient to reduce %5$s to an appropriately low "
"level (i.e., %5$s < %6$s%%)."
msgstr "%1$s\n\n感興趣之數量為母體中的錯報 %2$s。錯報定義為一項目之帳面（已記錄）數值與其審計（真實）數值之差異。當針對給定之績效重大性檢定母體錯報時，會針對 %2$s 建立兩個統計假設：\n\n- （虛無）假設 %3$s，\n- （對立）假設 %4$s。\n\n審計風險 %5$s 是不正確地拒絕假設 %3$s 之風險。為根據樣本拒絕此假設，樣本中之資訊必須足以將 %5$s 降至適當低之水準（即 %5$s < %6$s%%）。"

msgid ""
"%1$s\n"
"\n"
"In a Bayesian analysis, the parameter %2$s is assigned a prior probability "
"distribution that incorporates the available audit information about the "
"misstatement in the population."
msgstr "%1$s\n\n在貝氏分析中，參數 %2$s 被賦予一個整合了關於母體錯報之可用審計資訊的先驗機率分布。"

msgid "a performance materiality of %1$s"
msgstr "績效重大性 %1$s"

msgid ""
"the sample provides sufficient information to conclude that the misstatement "
"in the population is below the performance materiality"
msgstr "樣本提供足夠資訊以推論母體錯報低於績效重大性"

msgid "a minimum precision of %1$s"
msgstr "最小精確度 %1$s"

msgid ""
"the sample provides sufficient information to estimate the misstatement in "
"the population with the minimum precision"
msgstr "樣本提供足夠資訊以最小精確度估計母體錯報"

msgid "a performance materiality of %1$s and a minimum precision of %2$s"
msgstr "績效重大性 %1$s 及最小精確度 %2$s"

msgid ""
"the sample provides sufficient information to conclude that the misstatement "
"in the population is below the performance materiality with the minimum "
"precision"
msgstr "樣本提供足夠資訊以最小精確度推論母體錯報低於績效重大性"

msgid ""
"Furthermore, the uncertainty regarding θ will only be extrapolated over the "
"unseen part of the population. This requires the additional assumption that "
"the population taints are homogeneous."
msgstr "此外，關於 θ 之不確定性僅會外推至母體之未見部分。這需要額外的假設，即母體污染值為同質。"

msgid "gamma"
msgstr "伽瑪"

msgid "beta"
msgstr "貝他"

msgid "beta-binomial"
msgstr "貝他-二項"

msgid ""
"The purpose of the planning stage is to find a minimum sample size so that, "
"given a certain number of expected misstatements, the sample provides "
"sufficient information to achieve the specified sampling objectives."
msgstr "規劃階段之目的在於找出最小樣本規模，使在給定一定數目之期望錯報下，樣本提供足夠資訊以達成所指定之抽樣目標。"

msgid ""
"No assumptions are made about the most likely expected error in the sample."
msgstr "針對樣本中最可能之期望誤差，不作任何假設。"

msgid "The most likely expected error in the sample is expected to be %1$s."
msgstr "樣本中最可能之期望誤差預期為 %1$s。"

msgid ""
"%1$s%2$s The minimum sample size that is required for %3$s, assuming the "
"sample contains %4$s errors, is %5$s. This sample size is based on the %6$s "
"distribution, the a priori assumption that every value of the misstatement "
"is equally likely, and the given expected errors.\n"
"\n"
"Consequently, if the intended sample is evaluated and the sum of "
"(proportional) misstatements in the audited items is lower than (or equal "
"to) %7$s, %8$s. %9$s"
msgstr "%1$s%2$s 假定樣本包含 %4$s 個誤差，則 %3$s 所需之最小樣本規模為 %5$s。此樣本規模以 %6$s 分布、每個錯報數值皆同等可能之先驗假設，以及給定之期望誤差為基礎。\n\n因此，若對預定樣本進行評估，且受審項目中（比例）錯報之總和小於（或等於）%7$s，則 %8$s。%9$s"

msgid ""
"%1$s%2$s The minimum sample size that is required for %3$s, assuming the "
"sample contains %4$s errors, is %5$s. This sample size is based on the %6$s "
"distribution, the a priori assessments of inherent risk (<i>%7$s</i>), "
"control risk (<i>%8$s</i>) and analytical risk (<i>%9$s</i>) from the Audit "
"Risk Model, and the given expected errors.\n"
"\n"
"Consequently, if the intended sample is evaluated and the sum of "
"(proportional) misstatements in the audited items is lower than (or equal "
"to) %10$s, %11$s. %12$s"
msgstr "%1$s%2$s 假定樣本包含 %4$s 個誤差，則 %3$s 所需之最小樣本規模為 %5$s。此樣本規模以 %6$s 分布、來自審計風險模型之固有風險 (<i>%7$s</i>)、控制風險 (<i>%8$s</i>) 與分析風險 (<i>%9$s</i>) 之先驗評估，以及給定之期望誤差為基礎。\n\n因此，若對預定樣本進行評估，且受審項目中（比例）錯報之總和小於（或等於）%10$s，則 %11$s。%12$s"

msgid ""
"%1$s%2$s The minimum sample size that is required for %3$s, assuming the "
"sample contains %4$s errors, is %5$s. This sample size is based on the %6$s "
"distribution, the a priori assumption that tolerable misstatement is equally "
"likely to occur as intolerable misstatement, and the given expected errors.\n"
"\n"
"Consequently, if the intended sample is evaluated and the sum of "
"(proportional) misstatements in the audited items is lower than (or equal "
"to) %7$s, %8$s. %9$s"
msgstr "%1$s%2$s 假定樣本包含 %4$s 個誤差，則 %3$s 所需之最小樣本規模為 %5$s。此樣本規模以 %6$s 分布、可容忍錯報與不可容忍錯報同等可能發生之先驗假設，以及給定之期望誤差為基礎。\n\n因此，若對預定樣本進行評估，且受審項目中（比例）錯報之總和小於（或等於）%7$s，則 %8$s。%9$s"

msgid ""
"%1$s%2$s The minimum sample size that is required for %3$s, assuming the "
"sample contains %4$s errors, is %5$s. This sample size is based on the %6$s "
"distribution, the a priori assumption that an earlier sample of %7$s "
"transactions containing %8$s errors is seen, and the given expected errors.\n"
"\n"
"Consequently, if the intended sample is evaluated and the sum of "
"(proportional) misstatements in the audited items is lower than (or equal "
"to) %9$s, %10$s. %11$s"
msgstr "%1$s%2$s 假定樣本包含 %4$s 個誤差，則 %3$s 所需之最小樣本規模為 %5$s。此樣本規模以 %6$s 分布、先前一個包含 %8$s 個誤差之 %7$s 筆交易樣本之先驗假設，以及給定之期望誤差為基礎。\n\n因此，若對預定樣本進行評估，且受審項目中（比例）錯報之總和小於（或等於）%9$s，則 %10$s。%11$s"

msgid ""
"%1$s%2$s The minimum sample size that is required for %3$s, assuming the "
"sample contains %4$s errors, is %5$s. This sample size is based on the %6$s "
"distribution, the manually specified prior distribution, and the given "
"expected errors.\n"
"\n"
"Consequently, if the intended sample is evaluated and the sum of "
"(proportional) misstatements in the audited items is lower than (or equal "
"to) %7$s, %8$s. %9$s"
msgstr "%1$s%2$s 假定樣本包含 %4$s 個誤差，則 %3$s 所需之最小樣本規模為 %5$s。此樣本規模以 %6$s 分布、手動指定之先驗分布，以及給定之期望誤差為基礎。\n\n因此，若對預定樣本進行評估，且受審項目中（比例）錯報之總和小於（或等於）%7$s，則 %8$s。%9$s"

